# Python Virtual Environment & Caches
venv/
ENV/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/

# OS specific
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE specific
.idea/
.vscode/

# Recorded order book history (grows continuously; not source)
workspace/depth_history/
# Same reasoning: recorded positioning history is local data, not source. It is
# also the only copy that will ever exist past the exchange 30-day wall.
workspace/positioning_history/

# Recorder logs. Written by the scheduled tasks under pythonw.exe, which has no
# console to write to; runtime diagnostics, not source.
workspace/logs/

# Inbound TradingView webhook payloads. Runtime state, not source: whatever a
# caller posts lands here verbatim, so committing it turns any field they send
# into repository history. Regenerated by src/server.py on the next alert.
workspace/tradingview_signals.json

# Live order book snapshot, rewritten every 0.5-2s while ws_feed runs. It is
# true for about a second, so a committed copy records nothing and only keeps
# the tree dirty. server.py serves a waiting_for_feed state when it is absent.
workspace/depth_latest.json

# Same again for the liquidation cascade window: rewritten on every liquidation
# and on a 2s heartbeat, so a committed copy is stale on arrival. server.py
# serves waiting_for_feed when it is absent, which is the honest state.
workspace/liquidations_latest.json

# Deliberately NOT ignored: workspace/telemetry_latest.json. It changes only
# when the pipeline runs, and docs/AGENT_INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md points other
# tools at it as the worked example of the documented schema. Kept on purpose.

# Accumulating output of tools/liquidation_probe.py. Runtime observation log,
# appended across runs and days; regenerate by running the probe.
workspace/liquidation_probe.jsonl
